  m3_t: "Look for a separate high-turnout group (Klimek method)",
  m3_b: "The model splits the data into two groups, but both have ordinary turnout. It does not find the separate group at 80–100% turnout associated with some forms of manipulation.",
  m4_t: "Are round percentages unusually common? (Kobak method)",
  m4_b: "Whole percentages of turnout and vote share are no more common than expected from chance (all test scores ≤ 1.3). This check has limited sensitivity in small polling stations.",
